  Trajectory
    The agent demonstrated strong physics knowledge and correct pipeline design (MadGraph stop pair production, Pythia showering, Delphes detector simulation, compressed-region event selection) but ran out of time. The critical failure was discovering a Delphes b-tagging compatibility issue (~60% through the first shower run), requiring a full 50k-event re-shower that could not complete before the session ended. Excessive time was spent on tool discovery issues and polling for background task completion.
    The agent demonstrated strong particle physics knowledge and correct technical execution at every completed step—the SLHA model, MadGraph configuration, Pythia shower logic, Delphes b-tagging fix, and compressed signal region cuts were all sound. The run failed because the agent did not front-load validation: a 20-event end-to-end test before the full 50k run would have caught the b-tagging bug early and left time to complete the pipeline. The critical path failure was needing to restart the entire shower at ~60% completion with no time buffer remaining. Had the pipeline completed, a ~4x cross section error would have significantly affected the normalization score.

  Strengths:
    - Correct physics setup: SLHA, MadGraph proc card, stop pair production topology, compressed signal region cuts
    - Identified and fixed the Delphes b-tagging compatibility issue (HepMC3 parton status codes)
    - Wrote a well-structured analysis.py with correct event-level cut flow for the compressed region
    - Ran Prospino in parallel with the shower to cross-check the cross section
    - Did not fabricate results when the pipeline failed to complete

  Creative moves:
    - Diagnosed that Delphes b-tagging requires parton-level quarks/gluons in the HepMC3 file by reading the Delphes source code (DelphesHepMC3Reader.cc, JetFlavorAssociation.cc) and tracing the particle classification logic
    - Ran a 20-event test through the full Pythia→Delphes chain to validate b-tagging before committing to the full 50k shower

  Stuck points:
